From 2a2e9f4995fa65319aeacb07dc201dbf0e4a2477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 14:32:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spread the per-frame samples across the pixel under DLSS

With eight samples per pixel the crawling over the model's surface was as
strong as with one, which rules out Monte Carlo noise: every sample in a DLSS
frame was traced through the exact same sub-pixel point, so extra samples only
reduced lighting variance and never filtered texture or normal-map detail. That
detail then aliases to a different value each frame as the reported offset
moves, which is what reads as the surface undulating.

Samples now spread symmetrically around the offset reported to DLSS, so their
mean still matches what DLSS expects while the detail is filtered within the
frame. Samples / Frame now improves this artefact instead of leaving it
unchanged.

This mitigates rather than cures it: the textures carry no mipmaps and the ray
tracer always samples mip 0, so a pixel covering several texels aliases by
construction. The full fix is generated mips plus ray-cone texture LOD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SfcRdgEzpuV52YCuhdR5ty
---
 HLSL/PathTrace.hlsl | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/HLSL/PathTrace.hlsl b/HLSL/PathTrace.hlsl
index 254415b..e9fc7b6 100644
--- a/HLSL/PathTrace.hlsl
+++ b/HLSL/PathTrace.hlsl
@@ -322,12 +322,24 @@ void RayGen()
 
     for (uint sp = 0; sp < spp; ++sp)
     {
-        // Per-sample primary ray. Normally each sample gets its own random
-        // sub-pixel offset for anti-aliasing; under DLSS the whole frame uses
-        // the one offset DLSS was told about, and DLSS resolves the edges.
-        float2 jit = (prevParams.w > 0.5f)
-                   ? prevParams.yz
-                   : (float2(rnd(s), rnd(s)) - 0.5f);
+        // Per-sample primary ray offset.
+        //   Without DLSS: an independent random offset per sample (plain AA).
+        //   With DLSS: centred on the offset DLSS was told about. Taking every
+        //     sample at that exact point leaves texture and normal-map detail
+        //     unfiltered, so it aliases differently each frame and the surface
+        //     appears to crawl; spreading the samples symmetrically around the
+        //     reported offset filters that detail within the frame while the
+        //     mean still matches what DLSS expects.
+        float2 jit;
+        if (prevParams.w > 0.5f)
+        {
+            jit = prevParams.yz;
+            if (spp > 1u) jit += float2(rnd(s), rnd(s)) - 0.5f;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            jit = float2(rnd(s), rnd(s)) - 0.5f;
+        }
         float2 suv = (float2(pix) + 0.5f + jit) / float2(dim);
         float2 sndc = float2(suv.x * 2.0f - 1.0f, 1.0f - suv.y * 2.0f);
         float4 sfarW = mul(float4(sndc, 1.0f, 1.0f), invViewProj); sfarW /= sfarW.w;
